[block'ORD-0003-graph'
  [ctx'the spec of EMS-003','.guidelines/.orders/EMS-003/EMS-003.pgml']
  [ctx'the signed model','.guidelines/.orders/INTAKE-2D-VIEW.md, section 6']
  [tgt'the graph of a package, derived from the tree and from nothing else: its nodes, its containers and its typed connectors, the same for the same source every time']
  [ins'derive a node from each Command and each Literal, a container from each section, block, part and segment, and a connector from each edge of the tree, typed by the operator that wrote it']
  [ins'derive the connectors the tree holds outside its edges: the sequence between siblings, the reference from a literal to the command that binds its name, the result a literal names after a nest, and the call of a template to its definition']
  [req'every node carries the source span of the command it is, so the view and the source point at each other']
  [req'a diagnostic lands on the node it is about: fix, ask and note, and an empty slot shows as a socket that asks, as needs does in the XML']
  [cnst'the graph is a function of the tree: it holds no fact the tree does not hold, and where the signed model puts binds and ref in the envelope, they enter the envelope first']
  [cnst'what moves an emitted projection moves by decision, written in .decisions, and enters the batch the version moves once for']
  [val'the derivation','for every declared source of the snapshot the graph is derived twice to the same bytes, and the tree is rebuilt from the graph to the same envelope']
  [val'the types','each connector type of the signed table has a case that shows it, and a tree edge of a kind the table does not name is refused by name, each seen failing before it counts']
  [val'the engines','where the signed model computes the graph in the engine, the Rust answers the same bytes as the JS over the oracle']
];
